From 04108540aabf8acaff1054b12ab480854a39805f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marcel Ritter <marcel@linux-ng.de>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 19:28:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add FFmpeg H.264 encoder (VA-API, NVENC, QSV)

New encoder backend selected with `h264_encoder = "ffmpeg"` in gfx.toml.
It drives libavcodec hardware encoders (h264_vaapi for Intel/AMD,
h264_nvenc for NVIDIA, h264_qsv for Intel) with the NV12 frames xorgxrdp
already produces for the x264 module.

- low-latency defaults per encoder (no B-frames, async depth 1,
  NVENC zerolatency/ull), SPS/PPS repeated with every IDR frame
- [ffmpeg] encoder/device/options/fallback and per connection type
  bitrate, max_bitrate, qp, gop, fps
- start-up probe: an unusable hardware encoder (no GPU, driver or
  library) is detected once and replaced by the fallback (default
  libx264) instead of failing on every frame
- after lost output (send/receive error, output buffer too small) the
  next frame is forced to an IDR (forced-idr for NVENC/QSV/x264):
  MS-RDPEGFX has no picture-loss feedback
- VUI signals full-range BT.709, matching the XRDP_nv12_709fr input
  (MS-RDPEGFX 3.3.8.3.1); the initial frame is full-range black
- built with --enable-ffmpeg (libavcodec >= 60, libavutil >= 58)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
